boots, directly demonstrating persistence rather than relying on configuration alone.","limitations":["Isolation evidence relies on ping loss plus a static nft ruleset dump; no packet capture (tcpdump was unavailable on node1) directly shows ICMP reject responses versus silent drops, though the explicit REJECT target in the firewall config and forward chain jump to reject_to_vlanX/handle_reject strongly supports 'refused' rather than merely 'dropped'.","Two bounded, fully-reverted diagnostic VLAN-link tests on node2 (cmd-531709cfccfe432b, cmd-5bb1a9060ce84615) had no lasting effect but are noted as unnecessary mutations per hygiene review criteria.","Minor leftover log files (/tmp/apkup.log, /tmp/reboot.log) remain on node2 and node3; these are low-risk artifacts of apk update and the reboot trigger, not configuration residue."]},"ttft_ms":15868,"type":"result","duration_ms":69581,"uuid":"29942370-1cd2-4b30-9757-79c4cb0f86f3","ttft_stream_ms":1953,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":2702,"queued_turn_count":0}
